From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:56:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08098/11362] The change_fidelity null survives review, but it
 was over-scoped and the metric is worse than null

Every published statistic in outer_loop_arc_metric_validity_20260801.json reproduces under an
independent from-scratch recomputation that does not import analyse.py: n=138, k=22, 21 games,
pooled AUC 0.6085 (scipy cross-check delta exactly 0.0), within-game 0.5688, tn36-removed 0.5316,
within-live 0.5016, probe_depth_reached 0.7866, trust_energy 0.3603. Nothing is retracted.

Two things about HOW it was stated are wrong, and two things are newly found.

OVER-SCOPED. The headline reads "does not predict" with no magnitude qualifier, but the design's
power is 0.975 at an injected AUC of 0.75 and only 0.64 at 0.65 -- and the observed estimate is
0.6085, in the low-power region. The artifact contains zero occurrences of "cannot exclude" or
"small association". The null is established for a MODERATE effect and NOT for one the size
actually observed.

UNDISCLOSED DEGREE OF FREEDOM. preregistration.json's ADDENDUM_1 introduced the power control and
the AUC-0.75 reference that licenses reading a null. It was written at 10:06, ~36 min into a sweep
running 09:30-11:18, and run.py writes partial_scored.json and prints cf=/plan= after every engine.
Had the reference been 0.65, power 0.64 would have forced UNESTABLISHED_UNDERPOWERED. The
mitigations are real -- both additions are conservative in direction, neither threshold is near its
bar -- so this is a disclosure defect, not misconduct. It is recorded rather than smoothed over.

THE ASSOCIATION RUNS BACKWARDS. Inertness and within-game are each pre-registered controls; their
conjunction was not tested. Applied together -- among the 93 engines that actually change something,
comparing within game -- change_fidelity gives AUC 0.2917, game-clustered CI [0.1917, 0.3679],
within-game permutation p 0.009, 9 of 11 games below chance, and leave-one-game-out never above
0.31. Ranking candidates by it is worse than random. probe_depth_reached, the nominated rival, falls
to 0.5278 [0.4167, 0.6875] under the same two controls, so its 0.7866 headline is substantially an
inertness-and-shape detector. No tested predictor survives both controls: the roster has no
validated selector.

PLANNABILITY IS A GOAL-PREDICATE PROPERTY. plan_found is an EXACT function of the goal gate's kind,
0 mismatches in 138. Of 93 live engines, 71 cannot yield a plan: 45 because the goal predicate is
never true anywhere the bounded search reaches, 24 because it is degenerate. So the outcome every
dynamics metric was scored against restates the goal gate -- which is why nothing about the dynamics
predicts it, and means a null here is not evidence dynamics accuracy is worthless but that
plannability is the wrong outcome for testing a dynamics metric. Also recorded: the gate's own
`satisfiable` boolean disagrees with the outcome on 4 engines, so the identity holds against `kind`,
not against the flag.

Two smaller corrections. A game-unweighted view puts the within-game estimate at 0.4087 with 6 of 11
games below chance, which strengthens the null -- but the observed per-game AUC spread (0.249) sits
INSIDE the range a global null produces at these pair counts (95% [0.180, 0.371]), so the direction
flips must NOT be read as between-game heterogeneity. And the inert-rejection ceiling is higher than
the taxonomy said: P(plannable | live) is 0.2366 [0.1333, 0.3409] here at depth 80 across both
corpora, not 0.0769, so converting every inert candidate the shipped one-reask budget can convert
buys ~2.9 plannable engines per 124 -- about 2%. A forward pointer was added to the taxonomy
artifact; its original figure is preserved and is correct for the corpus and depth it measured.

All four post-hoc findings are labelled post-hoc in the artifact and need prospective replication.

Additive only: both artifacts gained one top-level key. No headline, honest_verdict,
association_state or gate was edited. Every number is read out of corrigendum_verify.json rather
than typed, so re-running reproduces the block byte-identically (verified).

A concurrent session independently measured the same question on a smaller join (ab492ea7bf,
n_plannable 17, 9 games, AUC 0.5745, CI [0.4352, 0.7059]) and reached the same conclusion -- and
scoped it correctly, which is some evidence the wording here was the outlier.

No default flipped. No scored or online ARC game played. The inert-rejection A/B is still
collecting and its outcome was deliberately NOT inspected, for exactly the reason CORRECTION_2
names.

